ON","targets":["SWS_DM_00311","SWS_DM_00309","SWS_DM_00384"],"text":"Figure 8.2: UDS Transport Request Processing","why":[{"c":0.9,"m":"cached_context_sweep/agy","mod":"gemini-3.8-flash","r":"Indicate incoming message to transport manager","rel":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","role":"heuristic","t":["SWS_DM_00309"]},{"c":0.85,"m":"cached_context_sweep/agy","mod":"gemini-3.8-flash","r":"Forwarding received UDS message via HandleMessage","rel":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","role":"heuristic","t":["SWS_DM_00311"]},{"c":0.8,"m":"cached_context_sweep/agy","mod":"gemini-3.8-flash","r":"IndicationResult enumeration definition","rel":"API_IMPLEMENTATION","role":"heuristic","t":["SWS_DM_00384"]}]}],"page":"classes/cl_apext_diag_uds_transport_UdsTransportProtocolMgr_83bb5e.html","used":[{"id":"SNIP_diag_AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_D_P69_017","sr":"Beleg aus AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Diagnostics (Seite 69) für diag."},{"id":"SNIP_diag_AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_D_P69_018","sr":"Beleg aus AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Diagnostics (Seite 69) für diag."},{"id":"SNIP_diag_AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_D_P69_022","sr":"Beleg aus AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Diagnostics (Seite 69) für diag."},{"id":"SNIP_diag_AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_D_P78_055","sr":"Beleg aus AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Diagnostics (Seite 78) für diag."},{"id":"SNIP_diag_AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_D_P79_064","sr":"Beleg aus AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Diagnostics (Seite 79) für diag."},{"id":"SNIP_diag_AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_D_P81_067","sr":"Beleg aus AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Diagnostics (Seite 81) für diag."},{"id":"SNIP_diag_AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_D_P84_091","sr":"Beleg aus AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Diagnostics (Seite 84) für diag."},{"id":"SNIP_diag_AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_D_P95_128","sr":"Beleg aus AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Diagnostics (Seite 95) für diag.","text":"Specification of Diagnostics AUTOSAR AP R25-11 7.1.1 Support of UDS Transport Layer The UDS Transport Protocol API is formally described in section C. This section describes the required interaction of the components using this API. Each (propri- etary) UDS Transport Protocol implementation subclasses the abstract class apext:: diag::uds_transport::UdsTransportProtocolHandler , which shall be pro- vided by DM according to [SWS_DM_00315]. 7.1.1.1 Initialization, Starting and Stopping of a UDS TransportLayer [SWS_DM_00329] Lifecycle management of an UDS Transport Protocol imple- mentation Upstream requirements: RS_Diag_04168 ⌈ The lifecycle of an UDS Transport Protocol implementation shall be managed by the DM in the following order: • Creation of the UDS Transport Protocol implementation by calling its con- structor apext::diag::uds_transport::UdsTransportProtocolHan- dler::UdsTransportProtocolHandler . • Initializing of the UDS Transport Protocol implementation by calling apext:: diag::uds_transport::UdsTransportProtocolHandler::Initial- ize . • Starting of the UDS Transport Protocol implementation by calling apext:: diag::uds_transport::UdsTransportProtocolHandler::Start . • Stopping of the UDS Transport Protocol implementation by calling apext:: diag::uds_transport::UdsTransportProtocolHandler::Stop . ⌋ [SWS_DM_00330] Construction of an UDS Transport Protocol implementation Upstream requirements: RS_Diag_04168 ⌈ The DM shall call the specific constructor of the UDS Transport Protocol imple- mentation, where the argument handlerId is unique among all by DM instanti- ated UDS Transport Protocol implementations and the argument transportProto- colMgr is set to the reference of the instance of apext::diag::uds_transport:: UdsTransportProtocolMgr provided by DM. ⌋ [SWS_DM_00331] Initialization of an UDS Transport Protocol implementation Upstream requirements: RS_Diag_04168 ⌈ The DM shall call the apext::diag::uds_transport::UdsTransportProto- colHandler::Initialize during startup/initialization phase, before reporting Ap- plicationState.kRunning to the execution management. ⌋ 95 of 1171 Document ID 723: AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_Diagnostics"}],"v":1}
